<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick Augustus I of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1750–1827</span> · Also known as Frederick Augustus the Just, Frederick Augustus III, Elector of Saxony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick Augustus I was elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> from 1763 and became its first king in 1806 as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. The Treaty of Tilsit of 1807 also made him duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, a duchy he governed through ministers in Warsaw. He stayed loyal to Napoleon until he was taken prisoner after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leipzig">Battle of Leipzig</a> in 1813, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> took the duchy and much of Saxony from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-i-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Frederick Augustus I of Saxony" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcello Bacciarelli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederick_Augustus_I_of_Saxony_by_Marcello_Bacciarelli_(ca_1808-1809).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
